    "field": "Antarctic ice sheet climate modeling",
    "problem": "Existing studies of future Antarctic surface mass balance are limited by uncoupled climate models or downscaling techniques, lacking a fully integrated global framework to realistically simulate complex interactions between the atmosphere, ocean, sea ice, and the ice sheet itself.",
    "method": "This study uses the global, coupled Community Earth System Model (CESM) to simulate the Antarctic ice sheet's climate and surface mass balance from 1850 to 2100, forced by historical data and two future CMIP5 climate scenarios (RCP2.6 and RCP8.5) to project future changes.",
    "task": "The task is to simulate the past, present, and future climate and surface mass balance of the Antarctic ice sheet using the Community Earth System Model to understand and project its response to climate change.",
